{"source":"historical-basemaps","asOf":"2026-09-15","retrieved":"2026-10-14","licence":"GPL-3.0 (derived from historical-basemaps; this file stays under the GNU GPL v3)","note":"Borders: historical-basemaps by André Ourednik (GitHub aourednik/historical-basemaps, commit da7a4b7, GPL-3.0), snapshots 1500, 1530, 1650, 1715, 1783, 1815 and 1880; each holds until the next (1880 until 1886, where CShapes takes over). The project marks its borders as approximate. They show claimed territory: in many colonies European control reached only the coasts and a few inland areas, and small forts and trading posts are not drawn. Orbis assigned polities to the eight colonial powers by their names and overlords, corrected three errors (1783: Quebec British since 1763, Louisiana Spanish 1762-1801; 1815: Río de la Plata independent in fact since 1810), cut each empire into pieces with their own dates so gains can be highlighted, and simplified the shapes. The Dutch East Indies are drawn as the whole archipelago from 1650 (dashed): Dutch rule covered only parts of it until the late 19th century. This derived file is distributed under the GNU GPL v3.","groups":{"britain":{"label":"Britain","color":"c1"},"france":{"label":"France","color":"c2"},"spain":{"label":"Spain","color":"c3"},"portugal":{"label":"Portugal","color":"c4"},"netherlands":{"label":"The Netherlands","color":"c5"},"belgium":{"label":"Belgium","color":"c8"},"germany":{"label":"Germany","color":"c6"},"italy":{"label":"Italy","color":"c7"}},"topology":{"type":"Topology","arcs":[[[9010,17089],[91,13]],[[9101,17102],[40,-523],[-236,-3],[105,513]],[[4855,15245],[-77,-71]],[[4778,15174],[-31,-51]],[[4747,15123],[8,59],[100,63]],[[4351,13941],[-48,300],[11,47]],[[4314,14288],[209,64]],[[4523,14352],[-172,-411]],[[4593,14621],[56,231]],[[4649,14852],[98,271]],[[4855,15245],[-91,-317],[38,-197],[-209,-110]],[[4531,14532],[8,2],[-16,-182]],[[4314,14288],[193,709],[162,0],[109,177]],[[4593,14621],[-62,-89]],[[4302,17644],[252,-350],